.el .ds Aq '
.TH start-cli-server-trusted-keys-update 1  "update "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-server\-trusted\-keys\-update \- Rename a trusted key and set what it is trusted for
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli server trusted\-keys update\fR <\fB\-\-name\fR> <\fB\-\-marketplace\fR> <\fB\-\-os\fR> [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename a trusted key and set what it is trusted for
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name for the key; blank names each GPG key after its identity
.TP
\fB\-\-marketplace\fR \fI<MARKETPLACE>\fR
Whether to trust the key for packages
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-os\fR \fI<OS>\fR
Whether to trust the key for StartOS updates
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
ID of the trusted key, as listed
